<http://data.silknow.org/object/0762e042-f418-330e-90bc-b1604269c803>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Ribbon of painted silk taffeta and cut work. White taffeta ground wit a zig-zag pattern in which one element is delicately painted with a floral pattern and the other is punched with a filling like lace. Each one of these differs slightly. The cut areas appear first to have been painted with a light glue and the centre cut out. A piece of net has then been applied to the back and painted with white paint to simulate lace."@en , "Ribbon of painted silk taffeta, painted and cut by Anne Dunkin, England, ca. 1800"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/783fcfbe-6985-3e66-b3ff-e7a4dbd2b377> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Ribbon of painted silk taffeta, painted and cut by Anne Dunkin, England, ca. 1800"@en , "Ribbon of painted silk taffeta and cut work. White taffeta ground wit a zig-zag pattern in which one element is delicately painted with a floral pattern and the other is punched with a filling like lace. Each one of these differs slightly. The cut areas appear first to have been painted with a light glue and the centre cut out. A piece of net has then been applied to the back and painted with white paint to simulate lace."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/0762e042-f418-330e-90bc-b1604269c803/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/0762e042-f418-330e-90bc-b1604269c803/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/0762e042-f418-330e-90bc-b1604269c803/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/0762e042-f418-330e-90bc-b1604269c803/dimension/4> ;
